        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 48,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 49,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Multiply both sides of the equation by \\(2r-7\\) to eliminate the denominator:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7).\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 216,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 217,
        "char_start": 127,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 94,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 95,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Expand the right side of the equation:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 289,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 290,
        "char_start": 219,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 134,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 135,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Simplify the right side:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 403,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 404,
        "char_start": 292,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 186,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 187,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 459,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 460,
        "char_start": 406,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 214,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 215,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Combine like terms:\n\n\\[-2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 542,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 543,
        "char_start": 462,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 247,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 248,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Multiply the entire equation by -1 to simplify:\n\n\\[2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 608,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 609,
        "char_start": 545,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 274,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 275,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Factor the quadratic equation:\n\n\\[(2r - 7)(r - 4) = 0.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 717,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 718,
        "char_start": 611,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 318,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 319,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Set each factor equal to zero and solve for \\(r\\):\n\n\\[2r - 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad r - 4 = 0.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 811,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 812,
        "char_start": 720,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 356,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 357,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Solve each equation:\n\n\\[2r = 7 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad r = \\frac{7}{2},\\]\n\\[r = 4.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1493,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1494,
        "char_start": 814,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 676,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 677,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Check if these solutions are valid by substituting them back into the original equation. First, check \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{6\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 - 19\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7}{2\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot \\frac{49}{4} - \\frac{133}{2} - 7}{7 - 7} = \\frac{\\frac{294}{4} - \\frac{266}{4} - \\frac{28}{4}}{0} = \\frac{0}{0},\\]\n\nwhich is undefined. Therefore, \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\) is not a valid solution.\n\nNow, check \\(r = 4\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{6(4)^2 - 19(4) - 7}{2(4) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot 16 - 76 - 7}{8 - 7} = \\frac{96 - 76 - 7}{1} = \\frac{13}{1} = 13,\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[4(4) - 3 = 16 - 3 = 13.\\]\n\nSince both sides are equal, \\(r = 4\\) is a valid solution."
      }
    ]
