  "raw_text": "Step 1: Multiply both sides of the equation by \\(2r-7\\) to eliminate the denominator:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7).\\]\n\nStep 2: Expand the right side of the equation:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21.\\]\n\nStep 3: Simplify the right side:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21.\\]\n\nStep 4: Move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0.\\]\n\nStep 5: Combine like terms:\n\n\\[-2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0.\\]\n\nStep 6: Multiply the entire equation by -1 to simplify:\n\n\\[2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0.\\]\n\nStep 7: Factor the quadratic equation:\n\n\\[(2r - 7)(r - 4) = 0.\\]\n\nStep 8: Set each factor equal to zero and solve for \\(r\\):\n\n\\[2r - 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad r - 4 = 0.\\]\n\nStep 9: Solve each equation:\n\n\\[2r = 7 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad r = \\frac{7}{2},\\]\n\\[r = 4.\\]\n\nStep 10: Check if these solutions are valid by substituting them back into the original equation. First, check \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{6\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 - 19\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7}{2\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot \\frac{49}{4} - \\frac{133}{2} - 7}{7 - 7} = \\frac{\\frac{294}{4} - \\frac{266}{4} - \\frac{28}{4}}{0} = \\frac{0}{0},\\]\n\nwhich is undefined. Therefore, \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\) is not a valid solution.\n\nNow, check \\(r = 4\\):\n\n\\[\\frac{6(4)^2 - 19(4) - 7}{2(4) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot 16 - 76 - 7}{8 - 7} = \\frac{96 - 76 - 7}{1} = \\frac{13}{1} = 13,\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[4(4) - 3 = 16 - 3 = 13.\\]\n\nSince both sides are equal, \\(r = 4\\) is a valid solution.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4}<|im_end|>",
